- Within a `sextant` block, named for the instrument which reads a position, successive calls
- to `unpack` read one value after another. The position advances by the width of each value:
+ Innerhalb eines `sextant`-Blocks, benannt nach dem Instrument, das eine Position abliest, lesen
+ aufeinanderfolgende Aufrufe von `unpack` einen Wert nach dem anderen. Die Position rückt um die
+ Breite jedes Werts vor:

= to `unpack` read one value after another. The position advances by the width of each value:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val version = data.sextant:
+ val version = data.sextant:

-   val magic = unpack[B32]
+   val magic = unpack[B32]

-   unpack[U16]
+   unpack[U16]

=   unpack[U16]
- ```
+ ```

- Binary formats favor repeated sections, and an array of records is unpacked by its count. The
- result of `unpack[Array[Pair]]` is a function from the count to the array, so the array is read
- once the count is known:
+ Binärformate bevorzugen wiederholte Abschnitte, und ein Array von Datensätzen wird anhand seiner
+ Anzahl entpackt. Das Ergebnis von `unpack[Array[Pair]]` ist eine Funktion von der Anzahl zum
+ Array, sodass das Array gelesen wird, sobald die Anzahl bekannt ist:

= once the count is known:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- case class Pair(left: U16, right: U16)
+ case class Pair(left: U16, right: U16)

- object Pair:
+ object Pair:

-   given debufferable: (Pair is Debufferable) = Debufferable.derived
+   given debufferable: (Pair is Debufferable) = Debufferable.derived

- val count = hex"00010002000300040005000600070008".sextant:
+ val count = hex"00010002000300040005000600070008".sextant:

-   val pairs = unpack[Array[Pair]](4)
+   val pairs = unpack[Array[Pair]](4)

-   pairs.length
+   pairs.length

=   pairs.length
- ```
+ ```

=   pairs.length
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

=   pairs.length
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

=   pairs.length
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
